Route B (selfhost) -- allow ONE positional parameter on a dynamic-module entry
point, so a replacement can name the receiver.

Rung C was blocked here and nowhere else. A Route B replacement for an instance
method is compiled as a synthetic TOP-LEVEL function, so the only way it can
ever see the receiver is as an ordinary first parameter -- and the contract
refused any parameter at all, before the interpreter was ever reached.

Exactly one assumption changes. Still static, still no type parameters, still no
named parameters, and TWO positional parameters are still refused, so this
cannot quietly become a general arity change. No receiver intrinsic and no VM
change accompanies it: the experiment is whether the EXISTING calling convention
already delivers the receiver in argument 0.

It does, on the host, against the reference installer:

  C0  String value(RouteBThing self) => 'NEW-C0'   (self ignored)  -> NEW-C0
  C1  String value(RouteBThing self) => self.label                 -> NEW-C1

Contract pinned by probes/c_entrypoint_arity.sh (6/6), behaviour by
probes/c_receiver.sh (4/4).

Applies to third_party/dart @ 6b58bb3a, on top of 0001-patchable-static-calls.

---
diff --git a/pkg/dart2bytecode/lib/bytecode_generator.dart b/pkg/dart2bytecode/lib/bytecode_generator.dart
index 7ba96aed..4e9f93e2 100644
--- a/pkg/dart2bytecode/lib/bytecode_generator.dart
+++ b/pkg/dart2bytecode/lib/bytecode_generator.dart
@@ -729,12 +729,27 @@ class BytecodeGenerator extends RecursiveVisitor {
           if (dynModuleEntryPoint != null) {
             throw 'Duplicate Dynamic Module Entry Points: $dynModuleEntryPoint and $member';
           }
+          // Route B (selfhost): zero OR ONE positional parameter.
+          //
+          // The single relaxation being tested, and deliberately nothing more.
+          // A Route B replacement for an INSTANCE method is compiled as a
+          // synthetic top-level function, so the only way it can ever name the
+          // receiver is as an ordinary first parameter. Everything else about
+          // the contract is unchanged: still static, still no type parameters,
+          // still no named parameters, and two positional parameters are still
+          // refused so "relax the restriction" cannot quietly become a general
+          // arity change.
+          //
+          // No receiver intrinsic and no VM change accompanies this: the point
+          // is to find out whether the existing calling convention already
+          // delivers the receiver in argument 0.
           if (!(member is Procedure &&
               member.isStatic &&
               function.typeParameters.isEmpty &&
-              function.positionalParameters.isEmpty &&
+              function.positionalParameters.length <= 1 &&
               function.namedParameters.isEmpty)) {
-            throw 'Dynamic Module Entry Point should be a static no-argument method: $member';
+            throw 'Dynamic Module Entry Point should be a static method with '
+                'at most one positional parameter: $member';
           }
           dynModuleEntryPoint = member;
           bytecodeComponent.dynModuleEntryPoint = objectTable.getHandle(member);
